          up: {"title":"Spot the formatting errors (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Damian's three-page information sheet came with these instructions: <i>Arial throughout; 12 pt body text; 14 pt bold centred heading; single spacing; left-aligned body; one-inch margins; bullets for unordered items; numbering for steps; the title in a header and automatic page numbers in the footer of every page.</i> Here is what he did.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY decision that breaks the instructions or good practice.","lines":["1. Heading centred in Arial 14 pt bold.","2. Body text in Arial 12 pt on page 1, but Times New Roman 12 pt on pages 2 and 3.","3. The steps for logging in to the school portal numbered 1 to 5.","4. The items to bring to Sports Day shown as a bulleted list.","5. Left margin changed to 1.5 inches because \"the page looked better\".","6. Line spacing set to 1.0 with 6 pt of space after each paragraph.","7. Page numbers typed by hand on the last line of each page.","8. The title appears in the header of page 1 only.","9. The temperature shown as 30 °C, with the degree sign inserted from the Symbol tool.","10. The words \"must not\" in bold in one safety rule."],"correct":[1,4,6,7],"win":"Sharp eyes. Line 2 breaks consistency; line 5 changes a stated margin without a reason; line 7 types page numbers by hand instead of inserting the automatic field in the footer, so they will not update; line 8 puts the header on one page only. The rest follow the instructions. Line 6 is still single spacing, and bold on two key words is sparing emphasis.","miss":"Test every line three ways: does it match the stated instruction, is it consistent on every page, and does it use the proper software feature rather than a manual imitation?"}
